---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import Header from '../components/Header.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'

// Account & data deletion.
//
// Google Play requires a PUBLIC web URL where a user can request account and
// data deletion — reachable without installing the app and without signing in,
// so someone who has deleted the app (or can't get into it) still has a route.
// In-app deletion alone does not satisfy that requirement; this page is the URL
// declared in Play Console -> Data safety.
//
// Content is grounded in what the delete-account Edge Function actually does
// (union-supabase supabase/functions/delete-account/{orchestrator,service}.ts).
// If that behaviour changes, this page must change with it.
//
// STRUCTURE: mirrors privacy.astro exactly — title-block, then
// <main class="doc"> with a .toc aside and an <article class="prose">, and NO
// scoped <style> block. Those classes live in src/styles/global.css. The first
// version of this page invented its own layout with bare <section>/<h2> and
// borrowed class names from support.astro, whose styles are SCOPED to that
// component — so the page shipped unstyled. Follow the sibling pages here.

const toc = [
  { id: 'in-app', label: 'Delete it yourself' },
  { id: 'by-email', label: 'Ask us to delete it' },
  { id: 'what-goes', label: 'What gets deleted' },
  { id: 'partial', label: 'Deleting only some things' },
]
---

<Layout
  title="Delete your account"
  description="How to delete your Union account and the data held with it."
>
  <Header back />

  <section class="title-block">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">Your data</div>
      <h1>Delete your <em>account.</em></h1>
    </div>
    <dl class="meta">
      <dt>Questions</dt>
      <dd><a href="mailto:privacy@unionwith.app">privacy@unionwith.app</a></dd>
      <dt>Deleted within</dt>
      <dd>Straight away in the app</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <main class="doc">
    <aside class="toc" aria-label="Contents">
      <div class="lbl">Contents</div>
      <ol>
        {toc.map((t) => <li><a href={`#${t.id}`}>{t.label}</a></li>)}
      </ol>
    </aside>

    <article class="prose">
      <p class="lede">
        You can delete your Union account, and everything held with it, whenever
        you want. There are two ways to do it: yourself in the app, or by asking
        us.
      </p>

      <h2 id="in-app">
        <span class="h-num">§ 01</span>Delete it <em>yourself</em>
      </h2>
      <p>
        This is the quickest route, and it happens straight away — no waiting on
        us.
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>Open Union and go to <strong>Settings</strong>.</li>
        <li>Scroll to <strong>Delete Account</strong>.</li>
        <li>Confirm. Your account and its data are removed immediately.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        One thing worth knowing: deleting your account does <strong>not</strong>
        cancel a subscription bought through the App Store or Google Play. Those
        are managed by the store, not by us. To stop future payments, cancel the
        subscription in your Apple or Google account settings as well.
      </p>

      <h2 id="by-email">
        <span class="h-num">§ 02</span>Ask us to <em>delete it</em>
      </h2>
      <p>
        If you no longer have the app installed, or you can't sign in, write
        to <a class="inline" href="mailto:privacy@unionwith.app"
          >privacy@unionwith.app</a
        > from the email address you used for Union, and ask us to delete your
        account.
      </p>
      <p>
        We'll confirm the request and delete the account
        within <strong>30 days</strong>. We ask you to write from the registered address
        because it's the only way we can tell it's really your account — we won't
        delete an account on someone else's word.
      </p>

      <h2 id="what-goes">
        <span class="h-num">§ 03</span>What gets <em>deleted</em>
      </h2>
      <p>Deleting your account removes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your account and sign-in details</li>
        <li>Your journal entries, written and spoken</li>
        <li>Your voice recordings, including the stored audio files</li>
        <li>Prayers you wrote yourself</li>
        <li>Your saved prayers and verses</li>
        <li>Your check-ins and the prayers they suggested</li>
        <li>Your settings, including your tradition and reminder times</li>
        <li>Your notification tokens, so reminders stop</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Two things behave differently</h3>
      <p>We'd rather be plain about these than leave them implied.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Prayers you shared with someone.</strong> The links stop
          working and are no longer connected to you or your account.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Records we're required to keep.</strong> Purchase and billing
          records held by Apple, Google or our payment provider are theirs, kept
          for tax and accounting reasons. We can delete your Union account
          without being able to erase their records.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Deletion is permanent. We can't recover a deleted account, and there's no
        grace period once it's confirmed in the app — so if you only want a
        break, signing out is the gentler option.
      </p>

      <h2 id="partial">
        <span class="h-num">§ 04</span>Deleting only <em>some things</em>
      </h2>
      <p>
        You don't have to delete everything to delete something. Inside the app
        you can remove a single journal entry, a prayer you wrote, a voice
        recording, or a saved prayer or verse, and you can retract a prayer
        you've shared so the link stops working. Your account stays as it is.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you'd like a copy of your data, or want something removed that you
        can't reach in the app, write to <a
          class="inline"
          href="mailto:privacy@unionwith.app">privacy@unionwith.app</a
        >.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our <a class="inline" href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains what we
        collect and why.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
